        "content": "### Where this data comes from\n\nThe **host** device is the box Ladder99 itself runs on. The adapter's `host`\ndriver polls the OS every few seconds (`services/adapter/src/schemas/host/`),\nships the values to the MTConnect agent over SHDR, and the relay writes them to\nTimescaleDB. Grafana reads them back through the `public.history_float` view.\n\n| Panel | Path | Units |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CPU | `$device/CpuTotal` | percent |\n| Memory | `$device/MemoryUsed`, `$device/MemoryFree` | bytes |\n| Disk | `$device/DiskUsed`, `$device/DiskAvailable` | bytes |\n| Disk Use | `$device/DiskUse` | percent |\n| CPU Temperature | `$device/Temperature` | celsius |\n\n`Temperature` comes from `systeminformation`'s `cpuTemperature.main`, which is\nnot readable on every platform - an empty panel there is normal on Windows and\nin some containers, and is not a pipeline fault.\n\nEvery panel on this dashboard is a native React panel (`timeseries`, `stat`,\n`text`). Nothing here needs AngularJS, which Grafana disabled by default in v11\nand removed in v12.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Help",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
